BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 629.89 Tm (included internal Redis deployment uses password authentication but does not enable TLS. CORS) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 615.89 Tm (origins, ingress rules, and metrics access should be narrowed in production.) Tj ET
BT 0.08 0.16 0.27 rg /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 580.89 Tm (4. Local deployment) Tj ET
0.12 0.39 0.65 RG 1.3 w 54 574.89 m 130 574.89 l S
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 554.89 Tm (1. Install Node.js and pnpm versions supported by the workspace.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.89 Tm (2. Run `pnpm install`.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 512.89 Tm (3. Configure `DATABASE_URL` and `SESSION_SECRET` in the local environment. When exercising) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 498.89 Tm (the Redis-backed Socket.IO adapter, configure matching `REDIS_PASSWORD` and) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 484.89 Tm (credential-bearing `REDIS_URL` values.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 463.89 Tm (4. Build the shared database package with `pnpm run typecheck:libs` or the database package) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 449.89 Tm (build command.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 428.89 Tm (5. Apply the approved SQL migrations to the development database.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 407.89 Tm (6. Run the seed scripts appropriate to the desired data set.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 386.89 Tm (7. Start the API with `pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server run dev`.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.89 Tm (8. Start the web app with `pnpm --filter @workspace/hotel-management run dev`.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 344.89 Tm (9. Verify `GET /api/health`, `GET /api/metrics`, login, and a representative protected) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 330.89 Tm (request.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 309.89 Tm (The API health response should be machine-readable with status `ok`. The metrics endpoint is) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 295.89 Tm (intentionally unauthenticated; do not expose it publicly outside development.) Tj ET
BT 0.08 0.16 0.27 rg /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 260.89 Tm (5. Replit workflow deployment) Tj ET
0.12 0.39 0.65 RG 1.3 w 54 254.89 m 130 254.89 l S
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 234.89 Tm (Use the existing managed workflows rather than creating duplicate servers. Confirm the API workflow) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 220.89 Tm (binds to the configured port and that the web workflow points to the intended API route. After code,) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.89 Tm (package, or run-command changes:) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 185.89 Tm (1. Restart the affected workflow.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 164.89 Tm (2. Check workflow and browser console logs.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 143.89 Tm (3. Verify the health endpoint and the browser preview.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 122.89 Tm (4. Run the changed user flow through a real browser smoke test.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 101.89 Tm (Keep environment variables and secrets in the workspace's environment configuration. Never commit) Tj ET
