BT 0.28 0.33 0.39 rg /F2 7.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 807.89 Tm (NEXUS HMS DEPLOYMENT STRATEGY) Tj ET
0.12 0.39 0.65 RG 1 w 54 798.89 m 541.28 798.89 l S
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 775.89 Tm (The Redis Deployment requires `REDIS_PASSWORD`, and the API reads its credential-bearing `REDIS_URL`) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 761.89 Tm (from the Kubernetes Secret rather than the ConfigMap. A NetworkPolicy permits Redis ingress only from) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 747.89 Tm (API pods on TCP 6379, and a second policy denies all Redis egress. Redis and web containers) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 733.89 Tm (explicitly run as non-root, disallow privilege escalation, and drop all Linux capabilities; Redis) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 719.89 Tm (also uses a read-only root filesystem.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 698.89 Tm (The Redis adapter provides cross-replica Socket.IO delivery. The current API Deployment also has) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 684.89 Tm (required pod affinity that co-locates all API pods on one node so they can mount the 10Gi) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.89 Tm (ReadWriteOnce uploads PVC. This preserves the three-replica/HPA template within a single-node storage) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 656.89 Tm (boundary, but it limits node-failure resilience and scheduling capacity. Multi-node API placement) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 642.89 Tm (requires shared filesystem storage with a suitable access mode or object storage. The process-local) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 628.89 Tm (cache and EventEmitter2 event bus do not synchronize state between replicas; Redis is neither their) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 614.89 Tm (shared cache nor a durable EventBus.) Tj ET
BT 0.08 0.16 0.27 rg /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 579.89 Tm (8. Database migration and release order) Tj ET
0.12 0.39 0.65 RG 1.3 w 54 573.89 m 130 573.89 l S
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 553.89 Tm (1. Take or verify a database backup.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 532.89 Tm (2. Apply additive migrations in staging.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.89 Tm (3. Run schema and API builds.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 490.89 Tm (4. Run authorization, MFA, mobile, metrics, and critical reservation smoke tests.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 469.89 Tm (5. Apply the migration to production during the approved window.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 448.89 Tm (6. Deploy the compatible API and web artifacts.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 427.89 Tm (7. Verify health, metrics, login, MFA, and one representative workflow.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 406.89 Tm (8. Monitor errors and latency before announcing completion.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 385.89 Tm (Do not run destructive schema changes in the same release as an unverified application change. Prefer) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 371.89 Tm (expand, backfill, verify, migrate, and contract sequencing.) Tj ET
BT 0.08 0.16 0.27 rg /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.89 Tm (9. Networking and security controls) Tj ET
0.12 0.39 0.65 RG 1.3 w 54 330.89 m 130 330.89 l S
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 310.89 Tm (- Terminate TLS at the approved edge or ingress.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.89 Tm (- Allow database traffic only from the API runtime.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 268.89 Tm (- Allow Redis traffic only from API pods and deny Redis egress.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 247.89 Tm (- Restrict `/api/metrics` to the monitoring network.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 0.17 0.2 rg /F1 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 226.89 Tm (- Configure CORS to approved web origins.) Tj ET
